  "description": "<p>When a binary is retrieved, a Content-Disposition header including the filename is sent.  In 4.7.0, the filename now includes the datatype URI:</p>\n\n<p>Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"newname.jpg ^^ <a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string</a>\"; creation-date=\"Sat, 19 Nov 2016 22:58:17 GMT\"; modification-date=\"Tue, 22 Nov 2016 19:24:48 GMT\"; size=277448828</p>\n\n<p>This results in the browser treating the datatype URI as part of the filename.  The filename should simply be a string with the datatype URI removed.</p>\n\n<p>See <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/issues/1145\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/issues/1145</a></p>",
